   "subject": null,
   "section": null,
   "segment": 0,
   "text": "Based on the equation\n$$\\Delta \\mathrm{E}=-2.0 \\times 10^{-18} \\mathrm{~J}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_{2}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_{1}^{2}}\\right)$$\nthe wavelength of the light that must be absorbed to excite hydrogen electron from level $\\mathrm{n}=1$ to level $\\mathrm{n}=2$ will be ( $\\mathrm{h}=6.625 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{Js}, \\mathrm{C} =3 \\times 10^{8} \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$ )",
